Source: nw-fermi-sb480
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: SMART Board Linux Recovery Project <smartboard-linux@example.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: nw-fermi-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 2.8.4), ${misc:Depends}
Description: DKMS source for the NextWindow Fermi input module
 Builds the free, out-of-tree nw-fermi USB input module for every installed
 kernel that has matching headers. It contains no SMART or NextWindow binary.

Package: nwfermi-daemon-service
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, binutils, kmod, udev
Recommends: nw-fermi-dkms
Description: udev and systemd integration for a user-supplied NextWindow daemon
 Starts one NextWindow daemon for the single supported SMART Board SB480.
 A second compatible board is rejected deterministically and does not start
 another daemon.
 The proprietary daemon is deliberately not shipped: the administrator must
 install an original copy at the configured path.
